    "body": "## Summary\n- add a separate `SUSPEND_JOB_OWNER` account-enforcement flow for confirmed job reports\n- derive the target account from the reported job server-side instead of accepting arbitrary user ids\n- persist an immutable audit record with report, target, moderator, reason and timestamp\n- cancel the suspended account's remaining OPEN listings so stale offers do not remain discoverable\n- make existing login/JWT suspension enforcement effective immediately for the sanctioned account\n\n## Lifecycle / safety\n- reject suspension when the target participates in `IN_PROGRESS`, `COMPLETION_REQUESTED` or `DISPUTED` work\n- do not let this path suspend the acting moderator or any ADMIN account\n- keep account enforcement independent from listing enforcement, so a reviewed report can have explicit, separately audited decisions\n- do not touch escrow, live tracking or active assignments\n\n## Data / privacy\n- Flyway V27 adds only moderation audit metadata and user/report references\n- account-enforcement endpoints stay under the existing `/admin/job-reports` ROLE_ADMIN boundary\n- no exact location, route geometry or live-tracking data is added to moderation responses\n\n## Validation\nRun Maven verify, frontend lint/build, Flyway/PostgreSQL/runtime smoke and payments-ledger smoke. Do not merge unless required checks are green.",
